# oodar — Gen 1 C host
File: website/pulled/oodar.oot

Source: openOODA/oodar/docs/

## What it is

The Gen 1 host substrate. Tag v4.0.0. Compiled `.oo` binaries
link against `oo_*` symbols. Build entry is `gcc oodar.c`.
Public ABI is `oodar.h`. Shared types are `types.h`.

Six per-domain subdirs match std vocabulary: core, sec, fs,
net, hw, app. The umbrella translation unit includes the `.c`
files in dependency order. `qa/` is not part of the public ABI.
From source: `gcc oodar.c`. See `oodar/docs/BUILD_AND_INSTALL.oot`.

## Surface

| Subdir | Scope |
|--------|-------|
| `core/` | str, list, mem, math, meta |
| `sec/` | caps, Landlock, crypto, PQC |
| `fs/` | OS syscalls, print |
| `net/` | fetch, tls |
| `hw/` | GPU HIP/ROCm dispatch |
| `app/` | actor, FFI, HITL, telemetry |

C shims stay in oodar/. They must not leak into `std/`
(RULES.oot §1.14 Pillar 9).
